ideally in socially acceptable ways, but often in terms of delinquency, gang activity and so on. And I try to remind myself when things happen that are really troubling that, you know, everybody has a need to matter and that this will get expressed one way or the other. In August 2005, a huge storm hit the Gulf Coast of the United States. Hurricane Katrina, of course, caused devastating flooding and widespread destruction across Louisiana, Mississippi, and Alabama. In the aftermath of the disaster, people, had many basic needs. They needed shelter, they needed food, but they also needed to feel like they weren't abandoned. Talk about this idea that after a mass disaster, a huge problem,
